# Copy this file to .env and fill in a real RPC URL per chain.
# Never commit .env — it is gitignored.
#
# The AccessControl event-reconstruction path needs eth_getLogs over WIDE block
# ranges. NOTE: a paid tier is not automatically enough — a free Alchemy key
# (and public endpoints like blastapi) cap getLogs at ~10 blocks, and even
# Infura's 10k / Alchemy PAYG's 2k range leaves a deep-history contract as a
# labelled partial under the default request budget. `reconstruction.complete`
# is true only when the probed range covers the contract's whole history within
# the budget (~range >= history/750); otherwise Ripcord returns an explicitly
# labelled partial reconstruction, never a silent failure. For fast, single-pass,
# complete deep-history scans on the day-5 set, use an unbounded/large-range,
# un-rate-limited endpoint. The provider name (host only, never the key) is
# printed at the start of every scan.
#
# Determinism is provider-independent: every read is pinned to a block and
# cached by (chainId, block, method, params) — NOT by provider — so a warm
# cache built with one provider is a valid, identical hit for another.

RPC_URL_1=https://your-mainnet-rpc-provider.example/v2/YOUR_KEY
